  ```
- If it starts with `{` but you’re deserializing to `List<JobEntity>`, swap to `JobEntity`.

**How to confirm:** log the raw payload once (see #5).

---

### 2) The API returned HTML or plain text (error page, 500, auth redirect)
If the payload starts with `<` (or it isn’t JSON), you’ll get this exact error at byte 1.
- Check `response.IsSuccessStatusCode` before deserializing.
- If not success, log `await response.Content.ReadAsStringAsync()` and handle it.

---

### 3) Property casing / enum / converter issues
Even with the right shape, `System.Text.Json` can choke on common types.

Use a shared `JsonSerializerOptions`:

```csharp
var options = new JsonSerializerOptions
{
    PropertyNameCaseInsensitive = true
};
options.Converters.Add(new JsonStringEnumConverter());
// DateOnly/TimeOnly need converters unless you’re on .NET 8 with proper formatters
options.Converters.Add(new DateOnlyJsonConverter());
options.Converters.Add(new TimeOnlyJsonConverter());
```

Example `DateOnly` / `TimeOnly` converters (works on .NET 6/7):

```csharp
public sealed class DateOnlyJsonConverter : JsonConverter<DateOnly>
{
    private const string Format = "yyyy-MM-dd";
    public override DateOnly Read(ref Utf8JsonReader reader, Type typeToConvert, JsonSerializerOptions options)
        => DateOnly.ParseExact(reader.GetString() ?? "", Format, CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);
    public override void Write(Utf8JsonWriter writer, DateOnly value, JsonSerializerOptions options)
        => writer.WriteStringValue(value.ToString(Format, CultureInfo.InvariantCulture));
}

public sealed class TimeOnlyJsonConverter : JsonConverter<TimeOnly>
{
    private const string Format = "HH:mm:ss";
    public override TimeOnly Read(ref Utf8JsonReader reader, Type typeToConvert, JsonSerializerOptions options)
        => TimeOnly.ParseExact(reader.GetString() ?? "", Format, CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);
    public override void Write(Utf8JsonWriter writer, TimeOnly value, JsonSerializerOptions options)
        => writer.WriteStringValue(value.ToString(Format, CultureInfo.InvariantCulture));
}
```

